==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|it|cavatina}}, diminutive of {{m|it|cavata}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|music}} An [[operatic]] song in slow [[tempo]], either complete in itself or (e.g., in [[Bellini]] and [[Verdi]]) followed by a faster, more resolute section: hence
# {{lb|en|music}} A rather slow, song-like [[instrumental]] [[movement]]; the title, for example, of a movement in [[Beethoven]]'s [[string quartet]] in B flat, op. 130 (1826) and of a once-famous piece (originally for violin and piano) by [[Raff]], and of the slow movement of [[Rubra]]'s string [[quartet]] No. 2.

